            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<h2>Understanding the Real Costs of Air Purifiers</h2><p>Let's start with honesty: air purifiers aren't cheap, and neither are the filters you'll replace regularly. Understanding the complete cost picture helps you decide if one makes sense for your household.</p><p>Quality air purifiers range from $200 to $900 for the unit itself, though you can find solid options at lower price points. But here's what often gets overlooked: the filters. Most quality units need filter replacements running $20 to over $100 annually, depending on your specific model and how often you run it. If you choose carbon filters for odor control, budget for replacements every few months at $30-$50 each.</p><p>Energy costs matter, but perhaps less than you'd think. Modern air purifiers typically use 20-100 watts roughly the equivalent of a standard light bulb. Energy Star certified models are notably more efficient, costing about $30 less per year to operate compared to standard versions. If efficiency is important to you,<a href=\"https://claude.ai/chat/link-to-blueair-technology\"> Blueair's purifiers</a> are engineered to use less energy while delivering strong performance.</p><p>What You're Actually Paying For:</p><ul><li>Initial unit cost ($200-$900)</li><li>Filter replacements ($20-$100+ annually)</li><li>Electricity ($20-$40 per year, lower for efficient models)</li><li>Maintenance time (minimal, mostly filter changes)</li></ul><h2>How Air Purifiers Provide Health Benefits That Matter</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_KnqYBR": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
