            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-0",
            "max_width_desktop": "1096px",
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/image3_aae65b6e-eb23-4c54-a836-1e5e154e2cea.jpg",
            "image_desktop": "shopify://shop_images/image3_aae65b6e-eb23-4c54-a836-1e5e154e2cea.jpg",
            "caption": "",
            "caption_style": "p6",
            "product": ""
          }
        },
        "text_e9yarP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-lg",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Here's where the investment often starts to make sense. The average person spends roughly 90% of their time indoors, where something surprising happens: pollutant levels inside are often 2 to 5 times higher than outdoor air. In some cases especially with cooking, smoking, or during wildfire season indoor pollution can spike to 100 times higher than outside air.</p><p>The EPA consistently ranks indoor air pollution among the top five environmental health risks. That's not marketing, that's public health data. The effects are real: eye, nose, and throat irritation, headaches, respiratory issues, heart problems, and in serious cases, long-term health impacts.</p><p>Quality air purifiers address many of these concerns. Research shows they meaningfully reduce allergy symptoms, decrease asthma triggers, and improve overall respiratory health. If you have kids, elderly family members, or anyone with existing respiratory conditions, the difference in comfort and health can be substantial.</p><h3>Who notices the biggest benefits from air purifiers:</h3><p>Allergy sufferers - If pollen, dust mites, and pet dander trigger your symptoms, a HEPA-grade filter captures 99.97% of these particles.<a href=\"https://claude.ai/chat/link-to-hepassilent\"> Blueair's HEPASilent™ technology</a> goes further, filtering down to 0.1 microns while running significantly quieter than traditional HEPA units.</p><p>Parents - Nearly 1 in 13 school-age children has asthma. Reducing airborne triggers gives kids fewer sick days and better quality of life.</p><p>Pet owners - Air purifiers tackle the dander and odors that accumulate throughout your home, not just in the room where your pet spends time.</p><p>City dwellers - Higher outdoor pollution means more contaminants seeping into your home's indoor air, making air purifiers a practical defensive tool.</p><p>Anyone with respiratory conditions - Cleaner air literally means fewer triggers and easier breathing.</p><h2>What Air Purifiers Actually Remove and Their Limitations</h2><p>Setting realistic expectations prevents buyer's remorse. HEPA-grade filters excel at particles: dust, pollen, pet dander, mold spores, and fine particulates. Studies confirm HEPA filters capture 99.97% of particles at 0.3 micrometers. That's the science working.</p><p>However, limitations exist with air purifiers. Most filters handle particles better than gases. Volatile organic compounds (VOCs), radon, and carbon monoxide require specialized solutions upgraded carbon filters help with some odors, but they're not a complete fix for gaseous pollutants. And while some ionizers may produce ozone,<a href=\"https://claude.ai/chat/link-to-zero-ozone-cert\"> Blueair purifiers are CARB-certified for zero ozone emissions</a>, so that's not a concern with our products.</p><h2>The Long-Term Value Air Purifiers Deliver Beyond Immediate Health</h2><p>The value extends beyond breathing easier. Running an air purifier protects your HVAC system by reducing the dust and debris that would otherwise circulate through your blower motor and ductwork. Less strain means better efficiency, lower energy bills, and equipment that lasts longer.</p><p>You'll also notice less dust settling on your furniture, electronics, and shelves. That means less frequent deep cleaning and less wear on your belongings over time.</p><p>For homes in areas with poor air quality or during wildfire season, air purifiers create a clean air refuge inside your home. That peace of mind knowing your family is breathing cleaner air when outdoor conditions are poor has real value.</p><h2>How to Make Your Air Purifiers Investment Work Best</h2>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
